      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 Wiley-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Stereoselective electrosynthesis of the first individual (f,t A)- and (f,t C)-1,4-fullerene derivatives with a non-inherently chiral functionalization pattern is described, as well as the first example of an optically pure protected primary amino acid directly linked to the fullerene through only the chiral α-amino-acid carbon atom. An application of an auxiliary chiral nickel-Schiff base moiety as derivatizing agent allowed separation of (f,t A)- and (f,t C)-1,4-fullerene derivatives using an achiral stationary phase, a separation which has never been done before."
      },
